From e499bdd4c1efd416857cf11830bac398866cd547 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate deploy target from Vercel to Cloudflare Workers

- Add the OpenNext Cloudflare adapter (wrangler.jsonc, open-next.config.ts)
  as the recommended, production-ready way to run this Next.js app (with
  SSR, API routes and NextAuth middleware) on Cloudflare Workers.
- Replace @vercel/blob with a Cloudflare R2 bucket binding for product
  image storage.
- Replace sharp (native bindings, unsupported on the Workers runtime) with
  the Cloudflare Images binding for resize + webp conversion on upload.
- Bump next to 16.3.4 (OpenNext's minimum supported range).
- Add CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY.md with the full cutover: R2 buckets, secrets,
  first deploy, custom domain, Stripe webhook update, and finally removing
  the project from Vercel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
